/E (single parity bit: Suppose that the information to be sent, D in the Figure, has d bits. In an even parity scheme, the sender simply includes one additional bit and chooses its value such that the total number of 1s in the d + 1 bits \(the original information plus a parity bit\) is even. For odd parity schemes, the parity bit value is chosen such that there is an odd number of 1s. the Figure illustrates an even parity scheme, with the single parity bit being stored in a separate field.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
