/K [1]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 723 0 R
/E (Ethernet comes in many different flavors, such as 10BASE-T, 10BASE-2, 100BASE-T, 1000BASE-LX. 10GBASE-T and 40GBASE-T.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 724 0 R
/E (The first part of the acronym refers to the speed of the standard: 10, 100, 1000, or 10G, for 10 Megabit \(per second\), 100 Megabit, Gigabit, 10 Gigabit and 40 Gigibit Ethernet, respectively.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
394 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 725 0 R
/E <>
/Alt ()
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
395 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 726 0 R
/E (In most installations today, nodes are connected to a switch via point-topoint segments made of twisted-pair copper wires or fiber-optic cables)
/Alt ()
/Pg 37 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
396 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 727 0 R
/E (the switch itself is transparent to the hosts and routers in the subnet; that is, a host/router addresses a frame to another host/router \(rather than addressing the frame to the switch\) and sends the frame into the LAN, unaware that a switch will be receiving the frame and forwarding it.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
397 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 728 0 R
/E <>
/Alt ()
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
398 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 729 0 R
/E (Filtering is the switch function that determines whether a frame should be forwarded to some interface or should just be dropped.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
399 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 730 0 R
/E (Forwarding is the switch function that determines the interfaces to which a frame should be directed, and then moves the frame to those interfaces.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 731 0 R
/E (Switch filtering and forwarding are done with a switch table. The switch table contains entries for some, but not necessarily all, of the hosts and routers on a LAN.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
401 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 216 0 R
/Pg 38 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
